abstract: >-
  FreeFem++ scripts that model the generation of a tsunami by an earthquake and its propagation across the sea with a
  simplified Boussinesq system of Benjamin–Bona–Mahony type, solved by P1 finite elements and an explicit second-order
  Runge–Kutta scheme, over a flat bottom (the Mediterranean Sea), a bottom variable in space (the Java tsunami of 2006,
  generated passively) and a bottom variable in space and time (the same tsunami generated by the motion of the sea
  floor, from Okada's solution for 147 subfaults). The meshes are built from a picture or from bathymetric data, a
  domain adaptation technique follows the waves, and a test against an exact solution measures the rates of
  convergence.
